If you must use `awk`, you need to store the relationship between transcripts and genes first. This is a multi-pass approach:

```bash
awk -F'\t' '
# First pass: Map transcripts to genes
$3 ~ /(mRNA|transcript|transcript_gene_segment)/ {
    split($9, a, ";"); 
    for (i in a) {
        if (a[i] ~ /^ID=/) { split(a[i], id, "="); tid=id[2] }
        if (a[i] ~ /^Parent=/) { split(a[i], p, "="); gid=p[2] }
